1
00:00:00,377 --> 00:00:02,981
Tuesday. 2:59 AM.

2
00:00:03,058 --> 00:00:04,259
You're asleep.

3
00:00:04,335 --> 00:00:06,292
Your phone is face down on the nightstand.

4
00:00:06,449 --> 00:00:07,990
41 percent.

5
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:09,122
Across the hall,

6
00:00:09,169 --> 00:00:11,203
your little brother Leo fell asleep with his

7
00:00:11,096 --> 00:00:12,747
tablet on his chest.

8
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:15,686
Downstairs, there's the old landline your grandma refuses

9
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:16,628
to cancel.

10
00:00:16,592 --> 00:00:18,505
And at 3:00 AM exactly,

11
00:00:18,585 --> 00:00:20,291
all three of them ring.

12
00:00:20,253 --> 00:00:21,674
At the same time.

13
00:00:21,637 --> 00:00:23,145
Not just in your house.

14
00:00:23,108 --> 00:00:24,879
In every house on your street.

15
00:00:24,842 --> 00:00:26,219
In every city.

16
00:00:26,295 --> 00:00:27,847
On every continent.

17
00:00:27,925 --> 00:00:29,521
Eight billion phones.

18
00:00:29,596 --> 00:00:30,798
One ring.

19
00:00:30,875 --> 00:00:32,471
You turn yours over.

20
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:34,730
The caller ID doesn't say Unknown.

21
00:00:34,693 --> 00:00:37,122
It shows a number you know by heart.

22
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:38,155
Your own.

23
00:00:38,429 --> 00:00:41,076
Your thumb is already over the green button.

24
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,439
And then, downstairs,

25
00:00:42,486 --> 00:00:44,607
the landline stops ringing.

26
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:46,604
Because somebody just answered it.

27
00:00:47,114 --> 00:00:49,236
Nobody will ever fully explain what happened that

28
00:00:49,141 --> 00:00:50,025
week.

29
00:00:49,988 --> 00:00:51,551
But the people who made it to Monday

30
00:00:51,466 --> 00:00:53,380
all followed the same rules.

31
00:00:53,342 --> 00:00:54,631
Thirteen of them.

32
00:00:54,708 --> 00:00:56,260
Night by night.

33
00:00:56,337 --> 00:00:57,571
From the first ring,

34
00:00:57,684 --> 00:00:59,608
to the moment you realize who has been

35
00:00:59,513 --> 00:01:01,569
reading these rules to you.

36
00:01:01,532 --> 00:01:04,004
Night one. The first ring.

37
00:01:04,373 --> 00:01:05,552
At 3:00 AM,

38
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:08,291
the first thing everyone does is the same.

39
00:01:08,254 --> 00:01:09,587
They answer.

40
00:01:09,663 --> 00:01:11,391
Not because they're brave.

41
00:01:11,354 --> 00:01:13,464
Because a ringing phone is the oldest command

42
00:01:13,369 --> 00:01:14,702
we have.

43
00:01:15,448 --> 00:01:16,606
Rule one.

44
00:01:16,588 --> 00:01:19,235
Never answer a call from your own number.

45
00:01:19,198 --> 00:01:20,750
It isn't a glitch.

46
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:22,484
Your carrier didn't get hacked.

47
00:01:22,447 --> 00:01:24,251
Something is calling from the inside of the

48
00:01:24,145 --> 00:01:26,408
network, and it borrowed the one number it

49
00:01:26,303 --> 00:01:28,074
knew you would never block.

50
00:01:28,037 --> 00:01:29,151
Let it ring.

51
00:01:29,227 --> 00:01:31,699
It rings exactly thirteen times.

52
00:01:31,662 --> 00:01:33,138
Then the screen goes black,

53
00:01:33,097 --> 00:01:35,438
and the phone shows 41 percent again,

54
00:01:35,551 --> 00:01:37,289
as if nothing happened.

55
00:01:37,252 --> 00:01:38,355
But down the street,

56
00:01:38,271 --> 00:01:39,987
a dog starts barking.

57
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,108
Then another.

58
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,130
Then every dog in the neighborhood.

59
00:01:43,093 --> 00:01:44,864
And you hear your grandma's slippers on the

60
00:01:44,747 --> 00:01:45,785
stairs.

61
00:01:46,531 --> 00:01:47,864
Rule two.

62
00:01:47,846 --> 00:01:49,508
If someone in your house answered,

63
00:01:49,664 --> 00:01:51,808
do not ask them what they heard.

64
00:01:51,771 --> 00:01:53,760
Grandma is standing in the kitchen doorway,

65
00:01:53,775 --> 00:01:55,558
still holding the receiver.

66
00:01:55,521 --> 00:01:56,985
The cord is swinging.

67
00:01:56,948 --> 00:01:58,150
She's smiling.

68
00:01:58,225 --> 00:01:59,865
She says it was Grandpa.

69
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:01,862
He called to say he's coming home.

70
00:02:01,825 --> 00:02:04,123
Grandpa died in 2009.

71
00:02:04,086 --> 00:02:05,692
You want to ask what his voice sounded

72
00:02:05,587 --> 00:02:06,295
like.

73
00:02:06,258 --> 00:02:07,459
Don't.

74
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:10,651
The people who asked started hearing it too.

75
00:02:10,614 --> 00:02:12,779
Just take the receiver out of her hand.

76
00:02:12,742 --> 00:02:14,207
Put it back on the hook.

77
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:16,467
And unplug the cable from the wall.

78
00:02:17,213 --> 00:02:18,590
Rule three.

79
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:19,948
Before the sun comes up,

80
00:02:20,028 --> 00:02:21,920
agree on a family code word.

81
00:02:21,883 --> 00:02:23,172
In person.

82
00:02:23,249 --> 00:02:24,363
Out loud.

83
00:02:24,439 --> 00:02:25,662
Never over the phone,

84
00:02:25,819 --> 00:02:26,910
never in a text,

85
00:02:27,024 --> 00:02:28,444
never in a chat.

86
00:02:28,408 --> 00:02:30,299
Pick something nobody could guess from your life

87
00:02:30,192 --> 00:02:31,274
online.

88
00:02:31,237 --> 00:02:32,175
Not a pet.

89
00:02:32,252 --> 00:02:33,541
Not a street.

90
00:02:33,618 --> 00:02:35,170
Not a birthday.

91
00:02:35,246 --> 00:02:36,853
You and Leo pick a word at the

92
00:02:36,736 --> 00:02:38,047
kitchen table, whispering,

93
00:02:38,204 --> 00:02:39,646
like it's a game.

94
00:02:39,608 --> 00:02:41,073
It isn't a game.

95
00:02:41,037 --> 00:02:42,249
By the end of this week,

96
00:02:42,263 --> 00:02:43,903
it will be the only thing that tells

97
00:02:43,797 --> 00:02:45,437
you who is real.

98
00:02:45,399 --> 00:02:48,003
Day two. The ones who answered.

99
00:02:48,372 --> 00:02:50,142
In the morning the news says it was

100
00:02:50,047 --> 00:02:51,413
a solar storm.

101
00:02:51,376 --> 00:02:53,104
Then a software update.

102
00:02:53,067 --> 00:02:54,312
Then a hoax.

103
00:02:54,389 --> 00:02:56,269
By noon, nobody says anything,

104
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,065
because the people on the news start repeating

105
00:02:57,948 --> 00:02:59,095
themselves.

106
00:02:59,058 --> 00:03:00,259
Same sentence.

107
00:03:00,336 --> 00:03:01,844
Same smile.

108
00:03:01,921 --> 00:03:03,867
Every thirteen minutes.

109
00:03:03,943 --> 00:03:06,897
At school, half of Leo's class is missing.

110
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,025
At work, your boss sends a voice note

111
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,348
asking everyone to come in early tomorrow.

112
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,337
At 3:00 AM.

113
00:03:13,083 --> 00:03:14,372
Rule four.

114
00:03:14,355 --> 00:03:16,564
Never say the word yes on the phone.

115
00:03:16,526 --> 00:03:17,772
Not to a friend.

116
00:03:17,735 --> 00:03:19,243
Not to your mom.

117
00:03:19,207 --> 00:03:21,164
Not to a robot asking if you can

118
00:03:21,079 --> 00:03:22,205
hear it.

119
00:03:22,168 --> 00:03:24,158
Scammers used this trick for years.

120
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,826
They'd record your yes and use it to

121
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,469
sign you up for things you never agreed

122
00:03:27,352 --> 00:03:28,301
to.

123
00:03:28,264 --> 00:03:30,298
The thing on the line does the same.

124
00:03:30,261 --> 00:03:31,967
Only it isn't signing you up for a

125
00:03:31,849 --> 00:03:33,127
subscription.

126
00:03:33,092 --> 00:03:34,775
If you have to answer a question,

127
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:36,002
say correct.

128
00:03:35,964 --> 00:03:37,735
Or say nothing at all.

129
00:03:38,482 --> 00:03:39,684
Rule five.

130
00:03:39,665 --> 00:03:41,217
Turn off your voicemail.

131
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,207
All of it.

132
00:03:42,283 --> 00:03:44,766
Phone, landline, the old answering machine in the

133
00:03:44,649 --> 00:03:45,762
garage.

134
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:46,610
On Tuesday night,

135
00:03:46,482 --> 00:03:47,542
it calls.

136
00:03:47,504 --> 00:03:48,694
On Wednesday morning,

137
00:03:48,742 --> 00:03:50,326
there's a new message.

138
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,623
It's your voice.

139
00:03:51,699 --> 00:03:53,295
Your exact voice.

140
00:03:53,371 --> 00:03:55,416
Telling your own mom that you're fine,

141
00:03:55,495 --> 00:03:56,686
that you're coming over,

142
00:03:56,952 --> 00:04:00,356
and that she should leave the door unlocked.

143
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:03,054
Night three. The voices.

144
00:04:03,423 --> 00:04:04,592
On the third night,

145
00:04:04,639 --> 00:04:06,683
it stops using your number.

146
00:04:06,646 --> 00:04:08,374
It starts using theirs.

147
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,234
Rule six.

148
00:04:10,216 --> 00:04:11,702
If you get a text from someone in

149
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:12,436
the same room,

150
00:04:12,549 --> 00:04:13,324
look at them,

151
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,010
not at your screen.

152
00:04:14,973 --> 00:04:16,788
It's 2:40 AM.

153
00:04:16,864 --> 00:04:18,405
You and Leo are on the couch with

154
00:04:18,288 --> 00:04:19,468
the lights off.

155
00:04:19,431 --> 00:04:20,983
Your phone buzzes.

156
00:04:21,059 --> 00:04:22,129
It's from Leo.

157
00:04:22,206 --> 00:04:24,503
It says, don't look at me.

158
00:04:24,466 --> 00:04:25,668
You look up.

159
00:04:25,743 --> 00:04:27,602
Leo is staring at you.

160
00:04:27,565 --> 00:04:29,248
His phone is on the table.

161
00:04:29,212 --> 00:04:30,063
Screen off.

162
00:04:30,338 --> 00:04:31,846
He didn't send it.

163
00:04:32,592 --> 00:04:33,837
Rule seven.

164
00:04:33,819 --> 00:04:36,335
At night, phones sleep in the microwave.

165
00:04:36,298 --> 00:04:37,500
Switched off.

166
00:04:37,576 --> 00:04:38,734
Door closed.

167
00:04:38,810 --> 00:04:40,625
Unplugged from the wall.

168
00:04:40,589 --> 00:04:43,060
A microwave is basically a metal box,

169
00:04:43,075 --> 00:04:44,528
and a metal box is one of the

170
00:04:44,422 --> 00:04:46,609
few things that can block a signal.

171
00:04:46,573 --> 00:04:47,818
It's not perfect.

172
00:04:47,894 --> 00:04:49,074
But on the third night,

173
00:04:49,187 --> 00:04:51,637
the phone inside starts ringing anyway.

174
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,626
Muffled.

175
00:04:52,702 --> 00:04:54,385
Thirteen times.

176
00:04:54,462 --> 00:04:55,620
And then it stops,

177
00:04:55,667 --> 00:04:57,416
and it doesn't ring again.

178
00:04:57,379 --> 00:04:59,589
That's the first night you sleep.

179
00:05:00,335 --> 00:05:01,580
Rule eight.

180
00:05:01,562 --> 00:05:03,442
When someone you love calls you crying,

181
00:05:03,556 --> 00:05:05,305
ask for the code word.

182
00:05:05,268 --> 00:05:06,294
Every time.

183
00:05:06,370 --> 00:05:07,878
Even if it's your mom.

184
00:05:07,842 --> 00:05:09,657
Even if she sounds hurt.

185
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,654
Especially if she sounds hurt.

186
00:05:11,617 --> 00:05:12,874
At 4:10 AM,

187
00:05:12,745 --> 00:05:14,221
the landline rings.

188
00:05:14,183 --> 00:05:15,702
You plugged it back in to call the

189
00:05:15,596 --> 00:05:17,794
hospital, and you forgot.

190
00:05:17,758 --> 00:05:19,091
It's Leo's voice.

191
00:05:19,167 --> 00:05:20,412
He's crying.

192
00:05:20,489 --> 00:05:22,960
He says he's locked outside and it's cold.

193
00:05:22,924 --> 00:05:24,300
You turn around.

194
00:05:24,377 --> 00:05:26,236
Leo is asleep on the couch.

195
00:05:26,199 --> 00:05:27,860
You pick up the receiver anyway,

196
00:05:27,974 --> 00:05:29,723
and you ask for the word.

197
00:05:29,686 --> 00:05:31,325
The crying stops.

198
00:05:31,402 --> 00:05:32,559
And on the other end,

199
00:05:32,673 --> 00:05:35,714
very quietly, something starts to laugh.

200
00:05:35,676 --> 00:05:36,658
Hang up.

201
00:05:37,358 --> 00:05:39,830
Night five. It learns.

202
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,280
By the fifth night,

203
00:05:41,196 --> 00:05:42,891
it doesn't need to call.

204
00:05:42,854 --> 00:05:44,406
It needs recordings.

205
00:05:45,152 --> 00:05:46,309
Rule nine.

206
00:05:46,292 --> 00:05:47,931
Stop recording your voice.

207
00:05:47,894 --> 00:05:49,183
No voice notes.

208
00:05:49,259 --> 00:05:50,198
No videos.

209
00:05:50,275 --> 00:05:52,342
No smart speaker in the kitchen listening for

210
00:05:52,235 --> 00:05:53,316
its name.

211
00:05:53,279 --> 00:05:55,357
Every word you upload is another word it

212
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,846
can say in your voice.

213
00:05:56,809 --> 00:05:58,964
Three seconds of audio used to be enough

214
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:00,727
for a scammer to clone someone.

215
00:06:00,691 --> 00:06:02,067
It needs less.

216
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:04,062
You go through your phone that night and

217
00:06:03,956 --> 00:06:05,738
delete eight years of videos.

218
00:06:05,701 --> 00:06:06,727
Birthday parties.

219
00:06:06,803 --> 00:06:08,005
Concerts.

220
00:06:08,081 --> 00:06:09,984
Grandpa's last Christmas.

221
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:12,138
It hurts more than you expected.

222
00:06:12,884 --> 00:06:14,260
Rule ten.

223
00:06:14,242 --> 00:06:16,177
If a phone rings while it's switched off,

224
00:06:16,335 --> 00:06:17,722
leave the room.

225
00:06:17,686 --> 00:06:18,800
Don't check it.

226
00:06:18,875 --> 00:06:20,515
Don't pull the battery.

227
00:06:20,478 --> 00:06:23,170
Just leave and close the door behind you.

228
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,904
It's not the phone that's ringing.

229
00:06:24,867 --> 00:06:27,208
It's whatever is standing where the phone is.

230
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:29,199
Rule eleven.

231
00:06:29,181 --> 00:06:31,084
Between three and four AM,

232
00:06:31,131 --> 00:06:33,406
do not call emergency services.

233
00:06:33,369 --> 00:06:35,129
On Thursday, your neighbor Mr.

234
00:06:35,011 --> 00:06:36,542
Alvarez does.

235
00:06:36,505 --> 00:06:38,188
His wife fell on the stairs.

236
00:06:38,152 --> 00:06:40,405
The dispatcher answers on the first ring.

237
00:06:40,368 --> 00:06:42,183
She asks for the address.

238
00:06:42,146 --> 00:06:44,487
She asks if the front door is unlocked.

239
00:06:44,450 --> 00:06:46,156
She asks him to stay on the line

240
00:06:46,115 --> 00:06:48,587
and say yes if he understands.

241
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:49,795
He says yes.

242
00:06:49,872 --> 00:06:50,789
In the morning,

243
00:06:50,803 --> 00:06:53,220
the ambulance is still parked outside his house.

244
00:06:53,183 --> 00:06:54,297
Engine running.

245
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:55,749
Nobody inside.

246
00:06:56,449 --> 00:06:59,053
Night seven. The last call.

247
00:06:59,421 --> 00:07:00,578
On the seventh night,

248
00:07:00,658 --> 00:07:03,163
every phone on Earth goes silent.

249
00:07:03,126 --> 00:07:04,241
No signal.

250
00:07:04,317 --> 00:07:05,606
No internet.

251
00:07:05,683 --> 00:07:07,016
No dial tone.

252
00:07:07,092 --> 00:07:09,608
And somehow, that's worse.

253
00:07:10,354 --> 00:07:11,511
Rule twelve.

254
00:07:11,493 --> 00:07:14,359
Write down every number you need on paper.

255
00:07:14,324 --> 00:07:15,131
Mom.

256
00:07:15,207 --> 00:07:16,408
The doctor.

257
00:07:16,485 --> 00:07:17,730
The neighbors.

258
00:07:17,807 --> 00:07:19,665
And write the rules down too.

259
00:07:19,628 --> 00:07:20,742
In pen.

260
00:07:20,819 --> 00:07:22,634
In your own handwriting.

261
00:07:22,596 --> 00:07:24,082
Because on the seventh night,

262
00:07:24,042 --> 00:07:26,208
your phone turns on by itself.

263
00:07:26,171 --> 00:07:27,723
The Notes app is open.

264
00:07:27,686 --> 00:07:29,107
And the rules are there.

265
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,184
All of them.

266
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:32,163
Only a few words are different.

267
00:07:32,767 --> 00:07:34,483
At 2:59 AM,

268
00:07:34,497 --> 00:07:36,773
you find something in Grandma's nightstand.

269
00:07:36,736 --> 00:07:38,025
A notebook.

270
00:07:38,101 --> 00:07:39,653
The paper is yellow.

271
00:07:39,616 --> 00:07:42,175
The date on the first page is 1987.

272
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,692
It's the same rules.

273
00:07:43,655 --> 00:07:44,943
In her handwriting.

274
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,484
It happened before.

275
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,718
Only once.

276
00:07:47,794 --> 00:07:49,477
Only on landlines.

277
00:07:49,555 --> 00:07:51,151
And she survived it.

278
00:07:51,113 --> 00:07:52,271
On the last page,

279
00:07:52,285 --> 00:07:53,772
she wrote one more rule,

280
00:07:53,928 --> 00:07:55,688
underlined three times.

281
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:57,811
The last rule.

282
00:07:57,793 --> 00:08:00,189
Nothing real will ever ask you to keep

283
00:08:00,093 --> 00:08:01,098
listening.

284
00:08:01,061 --> 00:08:02,482
You read it twice.

285
00:08:02,444 --> 00:08:04,259
Then you realize what time it is.

286
00:08:04,223 --> 00:08:05,687
3:00 AM.

287
00:08:06,763 --> 00:08:08,753
So, let's be honest with each other.

288
00:08:08,717 --> 00:08:10,324
You've been listening to a voice reading you

289
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:12,328
rules for almost ten minutes.

290
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:13,888
A calm voice.

291
00:08:13,963 --> 00:08:15,756
A voice that sounds like it knows what

292
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:16,742
it's doing.

293
00:08:16,705 --> 00:08:18,333
You never once asked it for the code

294
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:18,958
word.

295
00:08:18,922 --> 00:08:21,175
It's 3:00 AM somewhere right now.

296
00:08:21,138 --> 00:08:22,340
Check your phone.

297
00:08:22,415 --> 00:08:24,405
If the caller ID shows your own number,

298
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:26,158
you already know what to do.

299
00:08:26,121 --> 00:08:28,034
And if you've figured out rule fourteen,

300
00:08:28,048 --> 00:08:29,513
write it in the comments.

301
00:08:29,476 --> 00:08:31,335
Just don't write your code word.
